cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "fancyfx: Publication-Ready Effect and Evaluation Plots for Models"
abstract: >-
  Turns fitted models into figures ready for a manuscript. Plots the effect of a
  predictor with a rug of the raw data stacked directly above it, so a bend in
  the curve can be read against how much data supports it. Works across model
  types: generalized additive models fitted with mgcv are shown as partial
  effects via gratia, and other models, including mixed and Bayesian ones, as
  predictions via marginaleffects. Also plots model evaluation for
  presence/absence models, and diagnostics that species distribution work
  relies on: spatial sorting bias, spatial thinning, projection uncertainty,
  extrapolation surfaces, and niche overlap.
